WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.583
For over a decade, Bernie Calderon
Magtalas has helped the Philippine

00:00:04.583 --> 00:00:09.737
Government decide which energy, transport,
and climate investments are worth making.

00:00:10.507 --> 00:00:15.734
He started at the Department of Energy in
2015, and is now a Supervising Economic

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:20.832
Development Specialist at the Department
of Economy, Planning, and Development.

00:00:21.602 --> 00:00:28.898
Thirty-four projects. USD 14.05 billion.
Airports, roads, rail, energy, and ports.

00:00:29.668 --> 00:00:34.913
All appraised under the ICC review
framework: financial and economic models;

00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:40.504
market, technical, social, environmental,
institutional, and gender analyses; and

00:00:40.504 --> 00:00:46.095
for Public-Private Partnership projects,
concessions, risk, and prequalification.

00:00:46.865 --> 00:00:51.812
Fifteen development partner programs.
Twelve consulting studies. Forty-eight

00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:55.782
bills, laws, and policies. And eight
national boards advised.

00:00:56.552 --> 00:01:02.694
He built the Philippines' first Regional
Infrastructure Development Index, and a

00:01:02.694 --> 00:01:07.069
model ranking 207 projects in a
USD 176 billion pipeline.

00:01:07.839 --> 00:01:12.745
A Waseda University graduate and JICA
scholar, he was a Congress Future Energy

00:01:12.745 --> 00:01:17.524
Leader of the World Energy Council, and
is part of SIPA's Regional Knowledge

00:01:17.524 --> 00:01:22.178
Network on Sustainable Infrastructure,
along with policymakers and experts

00:01:22.178 --> 00:01:23.562
across Southeast Asia.

00:01:24.332 --> 00:01:28.663
See the full portfolio at
bcmagtalas.github.io/Career-Portfolio.
